text:
My husband and I waited about an hour to be seated (I think there was a graduation that day. 
) Despite the long wait, the food was better than I expected! I had banana pancakes, my husband had the peanut butter chocolate chip pancakes and loved them. The pancakes were the best part of the meal, sausage and bacon were tasty as well.  Unfortunately the scrambled eggs were very dry, so I'd recommend a different style. Overall good breakfast food and our server was super attentive and accommodating the whole time we were there. 

We left full and happy. Not a fancy brunch place, but a good place for a tasty classic breakfast. I'd go back!
